unicode-tag-stdin(1) -- stdin-only unicode-tag for confined use
===============================================================

<!--
# Copyright (C) 2026 - 2026 ENCRYPTED SUPPORT LLC <adrelanos@whonix.org>
# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS

`unicode-tag-stdin` [`--json`]

## DESCRIPTION

unicode-tag-stdin is `unicode-tag`(1) restricted to standard input: it reads no
files and takes no path arguments, so it can run under a tight AppArmor profile
(named `unicode-tag-stdin`) that denies all data-file access. It is the tool the
tool-output neutralizer pipes untrusted text through. The tagging is identical
to `unicode-tag`(1).

## OPTIONS

* `--json`:
  Read a JSON request `{"unicode-tag-json": VALUE}` and write
  `{"unicode-tag-json-result": TAGGED}`, where every string in VALUE (object
  keys and values, at any depth) is tagged. One process tags a whole document,
  instead of one process per string.

## EXIT STATUS

0 on success; 1 on an unreadable standard input, a malformed `--json` request,
or a closed output pipe.

## SEE ALSO

`unicode-tag`(1)
